    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (82.05) stands as our premier offensive anchor. Despite facing a crafty lefty in Carlos Rod\u00f3n, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and a premium spot in the order, where his elite contact profile mitigates the platoon disadvantage. We are also capitalizing on the high-floor production of **Bryson Stott** (72.63), who draws a favorable matchup against the hittable Lucas Giolito. Given that Stolen Bases are our scarcest category, **Geraldo Perdomo** (62.69) is an essential start today; his leadoff role against Justin Wrobleski provides maximum opportunities for speed-based contribution, bolstered by a +10% order bonus that pushes his efficiency well into the \"Strong\" tier.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Daulton Varsho** (37.48), who ultimately fell below the floor due to an elite matchup against Chris Sale. While **Daulton Varsho** typically provides the speed we crave, the combination of a tough southpaw opponent and a -10% platoon penalty made him a liability today compared to our locked-in outfielders like **Jung Hoo Lee** (67.27) and **Taylor Ward** (65.63). Meanwhile, we continue to monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz** on the IL; with **Tyler Freeman** also inactive due to a team off-day, our depth is being tested. We are heavily reliant on the **Luis Arraez** (69.53) and **Matt Chapman** (66.58) duo against Coleman Crow to keep our AVG and power metrics stable, though we remain cautious of the \"Lineup Pending\" tags for **Will Smith**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Drew Gilbert**, as any late-scratch or order drop could necessitate a rapid re-evaluation of our daily caps.",
